.TH SINDOOK-INSPECT 1 "2026-08-15" "sindook 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-inspect \- show sealed-file metadata, no credentials needed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook inspect
[\fB\-json\fP] [\fB\-glob\fP \fIPATTERN\fP]... [\fIFILE\fP...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the public metadata of sealed files without any credentials:
format version, key slots, and KDF parameters. This reveals nothing an
attacker holding the file does not already have. Armored input is
detected automatically. Slot metadata is covered by the header MAC,
which only a key holder can verify, so treat the report as a claim
until the file opens.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-json\fP
machine-readable output, one JSON array
.TP
\fB\-glob\fP \fIPATTERN\fP
add files matched by a portable filesystem pattern, repeatable
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sindook inspect budget.xlsx.sindook
sindook inspect -json archive.tar.sindook
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-verify (1),
.BR sindook-rewrap (1)
